# Words split after a written hyphen and Break long words (reference/common/typography.md). Page area of 260 × 160
# from (20, 20). Each character measures 5 and each line, 12. A Table of 60 + 100 + 100 whose cells get
# Break long words from a rule, and two texts 100 wide.
#
# Row 1, 24 tall (two lines in every cell):
#   c1: "REF-2026-009812" (75) in 60: split after its second hyphen, "REF-2026-" (45) and "009812".
#   c2: an IBAN of 24 characters (120) in 100: no part of it fits, so it is cut at 20 characters, and the other 4.
#   c3: an address of 22 characters (110) in 100: cut at 20, and the other 2.
# Row 2, 24 tall:
#   d1: "IBAN ES762077" (65) in 60: the word after the space (40) fits in a line, so it moves to the next one whole
#       and is not cut.
#   d2 and d3: one line each, stretched to the row.
# hyphens: without Break long words. "físico-químico-matemático" (125) in 100: "físico-químico-" (75) and
#   "matemático" (50). Two lines: 24.
# optimal: Break long words with Line breaking: optimal: 30 characters (150) in 100: 20 and 10. Two lines: 24.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 300
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
		For element: Cell
			Typography:
				Break long words: new-line
		For element: Text
			Box:
				Width: 100
				Background: #EEF2F7
	Section:
		Table:
			Id: table
			Column sizes: 60 100 100
			Body rows:
				Row:
					Cell: REF-2026-009812
						Id: c1
					Cell: ES7620770024003102575766
						Id: c2
					Cell: ana.garcia@example.com
						Id: c3
				Row:
					Cell: IBAN ES762077
						Id: d1
					Cell: Transferencia
						Id: d2
					Cell: Pagado
						Id: d3
		Text: físico-químico-matemático
			Id: hyphens
		Text: 0123456789ABCDEFGHIJ0123456789
			Id: optimal
			Typography:
				Line breaking: optimal
				Break long words: new-line
